      {
        "attempt": 1,
        "status": "OK",
        "asr_text": "Other small studies found changes before planned self-awakening. In one, activity in a front part of the brain changed about 30 minutes before waking. In another short-nap study, heart rate began to rise about three minutes before waking. But this is not proof that the body can read an alarm with perfect accuracy. Most self-awakening studies asked people to choose a waking time and try to wake then without outside help. That is related to waking just before an alarm, but it is not exactly the same event. The real question is why the feeling can sometimes be so precise.",
